 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * Version 2.6.0: first release of this fork
    (https://github.com/speakzzz/BlackTools-TCL). Includes all fork
    changes listed below since the original 2.5.5
 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * Boss owners are warned by note when the bot can't save its data
    (user file folder, channel file folder or BlackTools FILES folder
    missing, not writable or full), and told again once it's fixed.
    Checked a minute after loading and every hour, using a real test
    write. New lang strings loader.3 and loader.4 (EN, RO, FR, ES)
  * Load/storage problems are only marked as reported once an owner
    was reached; otherwise they are retried every 5 minutes. Before,
    a bot started with -m (no owners yet) never sent the note
  * If a note can't be stored, owners who are online get a notice
 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * Boss owners now get a note when module, command or protection
    files fail to load and are skipped, and another once everything
    loads fine again. Notes are sent a minute after loading, only when
    the set of problems changes, in each owner's language, and not to
    owners with notes turned off
  * New lang strings loader.1 and loader.2 (EN, RO, FR, ES)
 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * Fixed BT.TCL.tcl failing to load (logged "can't read tmp" on every
    load): two leftover lines from the atomic-write change ran at load
    time. The .tcl commands were unaffected
 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * Settings changed from IRC (nick, realname, homechan, cmdchar, etc.)
    are now escaped correctly when written to eggdrop.conf or
    BlackTools.tcl. Values containing " \ $ [ or ] could previously
    leave the config unloadable, be saved wrongly, or run code when the
    config was loaded. One shared helper (config:quote) replaces the
    partial per-setting escaping
  * away: messages containing quotes are no longer sent with \"
  * nick: nicknames containing { } are no longer altered or rejected
 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * New blacktools:write_atomic: files are written to a temp file and
    renamed into place, so a crash or full disk can never leave them
    half-written or missing. Original permissions are kept
  * AutoUpdate now writes eggdrop.conf (twice during an update) and
    BlackTools.tcl this way instead of overwriting them in place
  * Editing eggdrop.conf from IRC (config:save) no longer deletes the
    file before replacing it, and keeps its permissions
  * .tcl load/unload use the shared helper
 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * Braced all 515 expr calls outside Addons/ (e.g. expr $a + 1 ->
    expr {$a + 1}) and turned 86 simple counters into incr. Braced
    expressions are compiled once instead of re-parsed on every call,
    and values from IRC or data files can no longer be evaluated as
    code inside an expression. No intended behavior change: each
    conversion was checked by running old and new forms side by side
 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * Loader: a module, command or protection file that fails to load is
    now logged (with line number) and skipped instead of killing the
    bot; a summary of problems is logged after loading. Core files
    (Core, Binds, Ban, Timers, language) are still required
  * Loader: fixed module names being misread when loading from the
    update backup folder (scripts/BT.backup), which broke the special
    handling of a failed AutoUpdate module during updates
  * Loader: files now load in a fixed (sorted) order on every system
 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * .tcl wget: HTTPS-only downloads via Tcl's http package (wget no longer
    needed), async so the bot does not block, 1 MB size limit, up to 3
    https redirects, rejects web pages and incomplete Tcl scripts, writes
    via temp file so partial downloads never appear in scripts/
  * .tcl wget/load/unload/info: script names are validated (no paths,
    no "..", must end in .tcl); load refuses missing files and BlackTools
  * .tcl wget: download errors go to the requester by notice instead of
    raw wget output in the channel; fixed wrong name in "already
    downloaded" message
  * eggdrop.conf is now written atomically and keeps its permissions
 2026-09-27 speakzzz  (fork: https://github.com/speakzzz/BlackTools-TCL)
  * AutoUpdate now downloads from this fork; source is configurable via
    black(update_owner), black(update_repo), black(update_branch)
  * AutoUpdate TLS: removed forced TLS 1.0; uses TLS 1.2/1.3, SNI and
    certificate verification (black(update_verify_cert))
  * github.tcl: branch/ref support, ref name validation, HTTP status checks
  * to implement X rejoin if not on channel [ pending ]
  * to implement "Excesive character protection" [ pending ]
  * to implement category TCL in witch you have all tcl and also .tcl info
    to get info like bind pub, flags, strings from that TCL. [ pending ]
  * to implement .update reinstall [ pending ]
